 "transcription": {
  "from": "the published article (PDF): Tables 1-3 from the text layer, checked against the rendered page; Figs. 4, 5, 6 and 8 from the vector drawing of the PDF (marker centers mapped through the tick marks); Fig. 20, a raster image, by a column-wise scan of the gray levels; the rest from the text",
  "checked_against_source": true,
  "note": "Figs. 4, 5, 6 and 8 are vector figures: each marker center was mapped linearly (Figs. 4, 5, 8) or logarithmically (Fig. 6) through the tick marks of its axes; the center of a triangle or pentagon marker was corrected by its offset from its legend label (0.7 pt for a triangle), which the cross-check between Fig. 4 (ICP-MS), Fig. 5 (Cl/Ca) and Fig. 6 (Cl and Ca) confirms to within 3 %. Reading precision: 0.005 mass % in Fig. 4, 0.0005 in Fig. 5, 0.03 % in Fig. 8, 1 % relative in Fig. 6 (log axis), 0.1 mm in depth; the values are plotted against the mid-depth of the ground section (1 mm for 0-2 mm, and so on). Fig. 20 is a raster image (940 x 868 px, 11.6 px per cm3, 199.5 px per decade): the boundaries between the gray-filled areas were read at chosen abscissae as the centers of the black boundary lines, precision about 0.15 cm3; an area thinner than about 0.4 cm3 cannot be told from its boundary lines and is missed. Fig. 21 (NaCl solution) is not transcribed."
 },
