 "notes": [
  "The GEMS calculation (Section 2, Section 3.3): GEM-Selektor with the PSI-GEMS (Nagra/PSI 01/01) database supplemented with the cement data of the paper's refs. [15-19] (Lothenbach and Winnefeld 2006; Matschei et al. 2007; Lothenbach et al. 2008; Balonis et al. 2010; Dilnesa et al. 2011), the Cemdata07 generation with the chloride AFm of Balonis 2010 and the iron AFm of Dilnesa 2011. C-S-H is a jennite-tobermorite solid solution of constant composition: no uptake of Al, sulfate or chloride, and no Mg for Ca substitution. The sea-water composition used in the calculation is not printed; Table 1 is the composition the paper gives. The model follows Loser et al. 2010 (ref. [20]) with 165 g/L NaCl.",
  "The authors read the sea-water axis as a depth axis: low amounts of sea water correspond to the unexposed interior, high amounts to the exposed surface; the model has no transport and is 'not time nor space related' (Section 2).",
  "The authors' own comparison (Section 3.4): the model predicts brucite together with thaumasite and ettringite, not separately at the surface as observed, which they attribute to an overestimated Mg mobility; it does not predict a CaCO3 layer but a small gradual increase of calcite towards the surface; it predicts the portlandite depletion and an ettringite- and thaumasite-rich zone, as observed; Friedel's salt is predicted deeper in sea water than in the NaCl solution because ettringite is more stable than Friedel's salt in the Mg and sulfate zones.",
  "Cross-checks the test suite can run: Fig. 5 Cl/Ca equals the ratio of Cl to Ca in Fig. 6 at the same depth to within 3 %; the ICP-MS series of Fig. 4 equals the Cl series of Fig. 6 to within 0.5 %; the GEMS cumulative_top of a phase equals the cumulative_bottom of the next phase at the same abscissa, except at 7000 mL where 1.5 cm3 is unassigned.",
  "Binder: a commercial CEM I 42.5 R (Blaine 362 m2/kg, SO3 3.00 %) with 44 kg/m3 limestone filler, cast in 2001. It is not the binder of DeWeerdt2011 (laboratory OPC = clinker interground with 3.7 % gypsum, Blaine 450 m2/kg) nor that of DeWeerdtJustnes2015 (CEM I 42.5 R, Blaine 552 m2/kg, SO3 3.81 %).",
  "Fig. 21 (the same paste with a 165 g/L NaCl solution) is not transcribed. Figs. 11-14 (EDS dot plots, several hundred points) are not transcribed; their reading by the authors is in phase_observations. Fig. 7 (TG/DTG curves) is not transcribed; Fig. 8 quantifies it.",
